{
 "answer": {
  "dropped": "Nine call sites (v1, v3, v4, x1, x2a, x2b, x2c, x3, x4) drop the handle in place: pthread_detach on the fresh pthread word, then release of both Arcs. Those threads run detached; their pairs are never read through a handle.",
  "kept_v2": "v2's caller keeps the handle in an owned local (outlined drop 0x15df8a0) and registers the worker; it is the only type-A handle not destroyed at its call site.",
  "readers": "Exactly two take-style join bodies exist: join_a 0x15b8810 (type-A cell) with one call site in 0x15ec360 consuming a stored handle's pair, and join_x5 0x5cf7550 with three call sites in two bodies that dispatch the returned pair. The only other pthread_join caller, 0x56467d0, joins a different, larger cell. No join body exists for the X4 cell type.",
  "spawns": "Each entry base is loaded by exactly one lea in .text, inside its own spawn body; each spawn body has exactly one direct call site.",
  "stored_x5": "x5's caller stores the fresh handle in a hash map inside the owner struct via insert body 0x5cf0700 and detaches only the value the insert displaces."
 },
 "artifact": {
  "bytes": 105896032,
  "path": "artifacts/node/115/hl-node",
