 "boundaries": [
  "The instruction-level data flow from v2's registered guard into the exact owner field the join consumer reads (+0xa0) is not traced; the v2 claim is the elimination form: it is the only type-A handle that survives its call site, and the only type-A join call site consumes a stored handle.",
  "Join-internal semantics (the CAS/take order) of join_x5 and of the x5 detach path are the subject of open PR #3074 and are not re-derived here; both bodies are pinned only as census nodes.",
  "Censuses cover direct (E8) calls and indirect calls through GOT slots; register-indirect calls (call *%reg) cannot be enumerated statically and are out of scope. No RELATIVE slot points at join_a or join_x5.",
  "The X4 cell layout remains as #3050 left it (only its finish-store idiom is classified); the no-join claim for X4 rests on the pthread_join caller census and the take-idiom census, not on the X4 layout."
 ],
